      "ImageDescription": {
        "value": "A weathered mooring bollard dominates the foreground of this nighttime harbor scene, its rusted metal base supporting tightly coiled loops of thick, frayed rope that has clearly endured years of use and exposure to the elements. The bollard sits on a concrete pier, with worn wooden pilings visible to the left and a section of railing on the right framing the composition. Beyond the pier, the dark water of the harbor stretches out, its surface gently rippled and reflecting the warm glow of distant shoreline lights - a mix of white, yellow, and green points of illumination that hint at a coastal town or port facility across the bay. The deep black sky above provides a stark contrast to the scattered lights, lending the scene a quiet, contemplative atmosphere typical of a working waterfront after dark in Sattahip, Thailand.",
        "source": "commons-desc-page"
      },
